      "Language": "pol",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A case of a 50 year-old woman with unstable angina is presented. During the exercise test performed at 5th day of hospitalisation T wave normalisation in leads III, aVF, V4-V6 was observed. The subsequent angiography revealed critical stenosis of the right coronary artery and percutaneous coronary intervention was performed. Following intervention there were no T wave changes during exercise."},
